From: Josh Hou <joshhou@google.com>
Date: Sun, 24 May 2026 09:54:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 40/49] Fix path traversal and missing ownership check in
 LocaleManagerService

The getOverrideLocaleConfig method in LocaleManagerService lacked an ownership
check, allowing unauthorized cross-package and cross-user disclosure of
app-specific locale configurations. Additionally, the packageName parameter was
used to construct a file path without proper validation, enabling path traversal
attacks.

This change adds the missing ownership and permission checks, ensuring that
only the app owner, installer, or apps with the READ_APP_SPECIFIC_LOCALES
permission can access the configuration. It also validates that the constructed
file path remains within the intended directory to prevent path traversal, and logs blocked attempts to SafetyNet.

Bug: 495409704
Test: atest LocaleManagerServiceTest and manual test
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX

TAG=agy
CONV=1df5aed4-e067-499d-af15-55319a43c2f4
Cherrypick-From: https://googleplex-android-review.googlesource.com/q/commit:606c6d0e609db00d6b51d9e5075f175801479bdd
